  "decision": "operator-decided 2026-10-04 (relayed by workspace-89 and the main session; greenlit for production after workspace-ec review): :8083 architect_critic runs -b 512 -ub 512 and --no-cache-idle-slots; serving_shape.vram_non_kv_gib 38.03 (derived at -ub 512).",
  "acknowledged": {
    "A-1": "Part A evidence is ONE rep per arm (UFH14-B4i, 3 conversations x 6 turns, ~20-30k): turn-2+ TTFT median 16.3 s OFF vs 66.4 s ON, same hit rate 0.81, same VRAM.",
    "A-2": "With --no-cache-idle-slots an idle conversation stays in the pool and is purged with NO RAM copy when the 393216 pool fills (unmeasured by B4i); its next turn re-prefills. The orchestrator's prefix credit withdraws credit when such a purge was possible.",
    "A-3": "Part B evidence (attached, not waived) was measured on c7f5ac9ad = v10 + 9 commits with GGML_CUDA_FA_MASK_SKIP=0 and GGML_CUDA_FA_SEQ_ROWS=0 (the v10 FA path), not on the v10 binary. Both arms were CAPPED at 20 min; request 3 never reached first token; the 4-decoding / >=300k state was not reached. Paired gains up to ~280k occupied cells: iterations 0.22-0.28x as long, decode while a prefill runs 3.5-4.3x (1.43/1.70/2.16 vs 0.40/0.48/0.51 tok/s); coherence text identical, coherence_gate PASS.",
    "A-4": "KNOWN COST, exceeding the <=20% the package expected: a SOLO shallow prefill is 26% slower (383.8 vs 518.0 tok/s) and its TTFT 35% longer (208.3 vs 154.2 s at ~80k). Follow-up that removes it: KVU-16g (Sarathi-style per-iteration prefill budget).",
    "A-5": "vram_non_kv_gib 38.03 is DERIVED and conservative: the arm measured load 47.81 vs 50.77 GiB (-2.96; the DFlash2 drafter compute buffer also scales with -ub). The v10 load peak at bring-up replaces it in a follow-up.",
